# Smoke test for the gates that are wired up so far: input, addition,
# multiplication over Beaver triples, and output.
#
# Computes (I1 + I2) * I2 + I1.
#
# A product of two fixed-point values carries 2 * L_BIT fractional bits, and
# bringing it back down is the job of the truncation gate, which is not
# implemented yet. Run this circuit with L_BIT=0 so that the wires hold plain
# integers and the result can be checked by hand:
#
#   CIRCUIT=circuit/smoke.netlist N_BIT=64 I_BIT=64 L_BIT=0 cargo run -- dealer
#   CIRCUIT=circuit/smoke.netlist N_BIT=64 I_BIT=64 L_BIT=0 cargo run -- party 0
#   CIRCUIT=circuit/smoke.netlist N_BIT=64 I_BIT=64 L_BIT=0 cargo run -- party 1
#
# With I1 = 7 and I2 = -5 the output is (7 + -5) * -5 + 7 = -3.
I1 P0
I2 P1
G1 + I1 I2
G2 * G1 I2
G3 + G2 I1
O1 G3
